      ":question/problem": "Calculate $X+Y+Z$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Z=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X+Y+Z & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3+(-1)+5 & 3+(-3)+4 \\\\ 2+0+(-4) & 5+(-2)+(-3) \\\\ 2+(-5)+(-2) & 0+1+(-5)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
